# Excluded from every Docker build context.
#
# ⚠️ node_modules is the load-bearing entry, not a size optimisation.
#
# Each Dockerfile installs dependencies in a `deps` stage, then the `builder`
# stage does `COPY packages/<svc> ./packages/<svc>`. Without this file that
# COPY overwrites the container's freshly-installed
# packages/<svc>/node_modules with the HOST's — and in a pnpm workspace those
# are symlinks into a Windows .pnpm store that does not exist in the image.
#
# The failure is not a missing-file error at COPY time; it surfaces much later
# as the build script failing with
#
#     Error: Cannot find module '/app/packages/<svc>/node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc'
#
# which reads like a missing devDependency rather than a clobbered install.
# (Measured 2026-09-23 while adding Dockerfiles for ms-inventory/ms-analytics;
# the three pre-existing Dockerfiles have the same hazard and are fixed by this
# file too.)
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated inside the image, and copying a host build in
# would let a stale dist/ silently ship instead of the one just compiled.
dist
.next
**/dist
**/.next
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Local state that must never be baked into an image.
.env
.env.local
**/.env
**/.env.local
data
**/data
!packages/admin/src/data
!packages/shared/database/src/seed/data
logs
**/logs
*.log

# Generated Prisma clients are rebuilt in the image by `prisma generate`;
# a host copy targets the host's platform binaries.
**/.prisma-*
**/node_modules/.prisma

# VCS, editor and OS noise.
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test and doc artefacts that no runtime image needs.
coverage
**/coverage
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
